response.content:
{
  "intent": "top_up",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "I'm sorry to hear your top-up was cancelled. If the payment was not completed, no money will be taken from your account, so no refund is needed. If the funds were deducted, the amount should be released back to your account automatically, though this can take a few working days depending on your bank. If you don't see the funds returned after that time, please let us know and we'll be happy to look into it for you."
}

{
  "intent": "suspicious_or_unrecognized_transactions",
  "urgency": "high",
  "reply": "I'm sorry to hear that — an unrecognized charge can be concerning. Please freeze or block your card immediately in the app or by contacting us, note the date and amount of the charge, and review your recent transactions for any others you don't recognize. We'll then open a dispute on the charge and investigate it with you."
}

{
  "intent": "card_pin_request",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "You can set or change your PIN through your mobile app or online banking under Card Settings, or by calling the number on the back of your card. If you'd like, I can walk you through the steps or help you find the nearest branch or ATM where you can set it in person."
}

{
  "intent": "exchange_rate",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "I'm sorry to hear the exchange rate applied to your card payment doesn't look right. Card payments made in a foreign currency are converted at the rate set by the card scheme (e.g., Visa or Mastercard) on the transaction date, which may differ slightly from the daily published rate. If you'd like us to review the specific transaction, please provide the date, amount, currency, and the last four digits of the card, and our team will check it and get back to you with the details."
}

{
  "intent": "atm_issues",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "Declines at an ATM can happen for a number of reasons, such as insufficient funds, daily withdrawal limits, exceeding your available balance, or a temporary security restriction. I can't see the specific reason from here, but please check your account balance and recent transactions, and if nothing explains it, contact us so we can review the card for any blocks or restrictions."
}

{
  "intent": "cash_withdrawal_not_recieved",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "I'm sorry you weren't able to get cash. This can happen if the ATM is out of service or has run out of cash, your daily withdrawal limit was reached, or the transaction was declined for security reasons. Please check your available balance and daily limit in your banking app, try a different ATM, and let us know the date, time, location, and amount so we can investigate the transaction for you."
}

{
  "intent": "pending_bank_transfer",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "Thank you for reaching out. Payments can take a few business days to appear, depending on the type of transfer and when it was submitted. You can check the status of the payment in your transaction history, where it will typically show as pending until it is completed. If it has been longer than the expected processing time for that payment type, please let us know the date and amount, and we'll be happy to look into it further."
}

{
  "intent": "transaction_history",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "I can help you look into that €1.00 charge. It may be a small service or transaction fee, but to confirm, could you tell me the date of the charge, the description shown on your statement, and which account or card it appeared on? Once I have those details, I'll explain what it's for and, if it's an error, guide you on the next steps to dispute it."
}

{
  "intent": "change_pin",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "Of course. You can set a new PIN for your card through your mobile app or online banking under card settings, or by calling the number on the back of your card. For security, please avoid easily guessed numbers and never share your PIN with anyone."
}

{
  "intent": "change_pin",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "You can change your card PIN in a few ways: 1) At any of our ATMs, insert your card and select 'Change PIN'; 2) Through your mobile or online banking app under Card Services; or 3) By visiting a branch with photo ID. If you've forgotten your current PIN, we can mail a PIN reminder to your registered address, or you can reset it via the app. Is there anything else I can help with?"
}

{
  "intent": "standing_order",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "Thank you for your message. If your GBP salary has already arrived in your account, no further setup is needed on our side — it will simply appear in your account balance and transaction history.\n\nIf you would like the salary to be set up as a recurring payment, the sender (your employer) would need to arrange that with us, either as a standing order or as a regular bank transfer. Please note that we are unable to set this up from this chat for security reasons.\n\nIf the amount is not showing in your balance, or if you need help verifying the payment, please let us know the date and value of the transfer and we can look into it with you."
}

{
  "intent": "transfer_not_received_by_recipient",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "I'm sorry to hear your transfer didn't go through. Could you please tell me the date, the amount, and the last four digits of the account or card involved? It's possible the transfer was simply declined or is still pending. We'll check the status and let you know of the next steps."
}

{
  "intent": "pending_cash_withdrawal",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "Thank you for reaching out. It sounds like your cash withdrawal was not completed at the ATM, but the authorisation is still showing as pending. These pending amounts usually drop off automatically once the ATM operator confirms the transaction was not completed, typically within a few business days, and no funds are actually taken in the meantime. If the pending status remains beyond that time or the money is debited from your account, please let us know and we will look into it further for you."
}

{
  "intent": "replacement_card_fee",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "Thank you for reaching out. The fee for a physical card depends on the card type and whether it is a new order or a replacement. Please check the pricing section of your account or app for the exact amount, or let us know which card you're referring to and we can provide more detail."
}

{
  "intent": "cash_withdrawal",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "Our ATMs abroad can dispense your home currency if the machine offers it as an option at the time of withdrawal. If the machine's local operator offers this, you can select your home currency and the conversion will be shown to you before you confirm. Please note that cash withdrawal and foreign currency charges may apply, based on your account terms - you can check the exact fees in your app or on our website. If the machine doesn't offer your home currency, you can withdraw local currency instead, and your bank will convert it at the rate shown. We'd recommend carrying a small amount of local cash as a backup while you're away."
}

{
  "intent": "top_up",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "I'm sorry your top-up didn't go through. Common reasons for a denial include insufficient funds on the source card, daily or transaction limits being reached, an expired or incorrect card number, or the payment being flagged for security checks. Could you confirm the date, approximate amount, and payment method you used? Please also check whether any notification was sent to your app or email. In the meantime, you can retry using another payment method or a smaller amount. If the issue continues, we may need to review the transaction with our payments team, which can take a few working days."
}

{
  "intent": "topping_up",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "Deposits made with an international card may be subject to fees charged by your card issuer, such as foreign transaction or currency conversion fees. Please check the fee schedule for your card and your card provider for the exact charges before making the deposit."
}

{
  "intent": "activate_card",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "I'd be happy to help you activate your new card. You can usually activate it via our mobile app by selecting your new card and choosing 'Activate card', or by calling the automated activation line on the number printed on your card's sticker. Once activated, you'll also be able to set your PIN. Is there anything else you need help with?"
}

{
  "intent": "activate_my_card",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "Congratulations on your new card! You can usually activate it through your mobile banking app or online banking, or by using any of our ATMs. If you have any trouble or need assistance, please let us know and we'll be happy to help."
}

{
  "intent": "card_expiry_status",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "Thank you for reaching out. Before your card's expiry date, we'll automatically send a replacement card to your registered address — no action is needed on your part. Once it arrives, you can activate it in your app or by following the instructions included with the card. Your PIN will remain the same unless you've requested a change. If your new card hasn't arrived within a few days of the expiry date, please let us know and we'll be happy to help."
}

{
  "intent": "card_expiry",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "In most cases, a replacement card is automatically issued and sent to you before your current card expires, so you don't need to order a new one. Please ensure your address on file is up to date so the card reaches you in time. If you haven't received a new card a few weeks before expiry, contact us and we'll be happy to help."
}

{
  "intent": "apple_pay",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "Thanks for reaching out. Not all card issuers allow their cards to be added to Apple Pay, and American Express cards are sometimes restricted depending on the card and region. Please check with American Express to confirm whether your card supports Apple Pay, and ensure your device and Wallet app are fully updated. If your card is supported and still won't add, we're happy to look into it further with you."
}

{
  "intent": "pin_change",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "For security reasons, we're unable to display your PIN in messages or emails. You can view or change your PIN securely in the mobile app under Card Settings > Manage PIN. If you've forgotten it, you can set a new PIN there as well, or let us know and we can guide you through the options available."
}

{
  "intent": "activate_my_card",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "Great news that you've found your card! If it was previously reported as lost or stolen, you'll need a replacement, as the found card will no longer work. To add a card to the app, go to Cards, tap Add Card or Add to Wallet, and follow the prompts to verify your details. If you haven't reported it missing, you can simply activate it in the app under Cards > Activate. If you run into any trouble, let us know and we'll be happy to help."
}

{
  "intent": "contactless_not_working",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "I'm sorry you're having trouble with contactless payments. Please check that your card is contactless-enabled (look for the contactless symbol), that it isn't expired, and that you're holding it flat against the terminal for a second or two. If it still doesn't work, try inserting the card and entering your PIN, and let us know so we can look into the issue further."
}

{
  "intent": "pending_top_up",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "Card top-ups can sometimes take a few business days to clear, depending on your card issuer. Please check the transaction status in your app or account statement. If it hasn't been credited after 5–7 business days, let us know and we can look into it with the payment details (date, amount, and last four digits of the card)."
}

{
  "intent": "pending_top_up",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "A pending status means your top-up has been received but hasn't been credited to your account yet. This is normal and can take a short while to complete, depending on the payment method and your bank's processing times. Please wait for it to be processed, and if it hasn't updated after a few working days, contact us and we'll check it for you."
}

{
  "intent": "top_up",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "You can top up using our mobile app, online banking, or by visiting a branch. Please note that top-up amounts are subject to daily and per-transaction limits. If you'd like to request a limit increase, our team can review this for you — please visit a branch with valid ID or contact us by phone."
}

{
  "intent": "transfer_not_received_by_recipient",
  "urgency": "medium",
  "reply": "Transfers between our members are usually instant, but depending on the recipient's bank, they can sometimes take up to 1 business day to clear. The money is on its way, so your friend should receive it shortly. If it hasn't arrived by then, please let us know and we can look into the transfer status for you."
}

{
  "intent": "general",
  "urgency": "low",
  "reply": "A virtual card is a digital version of your debit or credit card that exists only in your banking app — there's no plastic card. It has its own card number, expiry date, and security code, and can be used for online and contactless payments, often with the option to freeze it instantly or generate single-use numbers for added security. If you'd like one issued, please let us know and we can guide you through the process."
}
